 ## Official optimization problem
 
 Each job visits the common machine route, with the fixed processing durations in `instances/`. Each operation runs once, machine processing intervals do not overlap, and a predecessor completes before a successor starts. Minimize the latest completion time. Baseline outputs use nonnegative integer hours and `end = start + duration`.
 
-Instance A requires its QUBO to be solved using a quantum algorithm on hardware or a simulator. Instance B requires its QUBO to be solved using a QUBO solver; our plan uses VeloxQ. The implemented fixed-horizon time-indexed QUBO, exact weights, window bounds, feasibility argument, and classical reference algorithm are documented in [STAGE1_OFFLINE.md](docs/STAGE1_OFFLINE.md). Both required methods have now run locally; the refined settings and validation are recorded in docs/STAGE1_REFINEMENT.md. Both remote backends are on user hold.
+Instance A requires its QUBO to be solved using a quantum algorithm on hardware or a simulator; Instance B permits any QUBO solver. The selected outputs use Qiskit Aer QAOA simulation for both: A uses one bit and one layer at makespan 4 h; B uses three bits and two layers at makespan 8 h. The root schedules match the selected runs in `output/stage1-selected.json`.
+
+The selected `solver/sequence.py` QUBOs preserve all two earliest-start common job orders for A and all six for B, and compute every permutation cost classically before quantum execution. They exclude arbitrary idle time and independent machine orders; no scalable compilation or quantum advantage is claimed. B's three-bit minimum is scoped to distinct representation of all six common orders. This is separate from the three-bit H8 deadline-feasibility reduction retaining five machine orders, including a non-permutation order. See [STAGE1_COMPACT.md](docs/STAGE1_COMPACT.md) for the selected formulation and [the claim register](docs/STAGE2_CLAIM_REGISTER.md) for the distinct deadline reduction. Earlier time-indexed/domain-wall formulations and refinement runs remain documented in [STAGE1_OFFLINE.md](docs/STAGE1_OFFLINE.md) and [STAGE1_REFINEMENT.md](docs/STAGE1_REFINEMENT.md); they are retained comparison evidence.
 
